# Trivy Ignore File
# 
# Format: CVE-ID expires=YYYY-MM-DD ticket=JIRA/TICKET-ID reason="Justification"
#
# This file provides the audit trail required by FedRAMP for formally accepted risks.
# Each entry MUST have an expiration date and a ticket reference.
#
# Review this file during every release cycle. Expired entries must be re-evaluated.

# Example entries (remove if not applicable):
# CVE-2024-XXXX expires=2025-03-01 ticket=SENT-1234 reason="No upstream patch available in alpine:3.20; monitoring for patch"
# CVE-2024-YYYY expires=2025-06-15 ticket=SENT-5678 reason="Low severity in our threat model; compensating control: network isolation"

# Current ignores (none at this time - base images are kept up to date):
# This section intentionally left blank. Add entries only when absolutely necessary
# with documented POAM/ticket references and expiration dates.